NOTE on the four VACUOUS rows — an empty result set proves nothing, so they are called out
rather than counted as coverage:
  dm-current-orders / dm-latest-orders : every one of the 25 delivery_man-assigned orders in the
      dev DB is order_status='delivered'; these two endpoints serve non-terminal work only, so no
      read-only fixture can populate them. dm-order and dm-all-orders ARE populated (149 / 230 key
      paths, both IDENTICAL) and cover the delivery-man surface.
  vendor-canceled-orders (vendor 1) : vendor 1 has zero canceled orders. vendor26-canceled-orders
      IS populated (240 key paths, IDENTICAL) and covers the endpoint.
  vendor-pos-orders : the dev DB contains ZERO orders with order_type='pos', so this endpoint
      cannot be populated read-only at all. Covered instead by static read (POSController.php:164
      eager-loads 'customer' only) plus the mutation-confirmed relationLoaded guard test.
